{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an image-only model using ResNet50 as the image encoder, with no RNA encoder, aggregation, or fusion. The validation accuracy of 0.2079 and F1 score of 0.1718 are significantly lower than RNA-only baselines, suggesting image modality alone may not achieve competitive performance. However, the absence of direct comparisons to other image encoders or multimodal configurations leaves uncertainty about the potential of image data when combined with RNA features or alternative architectures."
}

